1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,444
You see, any association we have,
as soon as it begins to influence

2
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:23,778
society in any way, will immediately
be broken up, and its members

3
00:00:23,778 --> 00:00:30,000
will either be jailed or face
other forms of repression.

4
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,570
In short, they'll break up everything.
As I told you, the presidential

5
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:38,000
administration's directive is:
silence, like in a cemetery.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Anyone in the Russian Federation
who tries to bring people together—

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,481
even for a completely apolitical
group, say, a union of seamstresses

8
00:00:53,481 --> 00:00:59,122
who play guitar—will face this. As
soon as that union gains influence,

9
00:00:59,122 --> 00:01:04,442
and the authorities realize that
these seamstresses could suddenly

10
00:01:04,442 --> 00:01:10,003
decide they are a political party
and quickly reorganize as one, even

11
00:01:10,003 --> 00:01:15,000
though they started as a union
of guitar-playing seamstresses—

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,848
as soon as the group begins to take
on a substantial shape, it will be

13
00:01:21,848 --> 00:01:24,000
shut down immediately.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,447
They'll find a pretext. Silence,
like in a cemetery. Don't stick your

15
00:01:29,447 --> 00:01:33,000
head out; it will be
knocked off immediately.

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,555
Anyone who tries to gather people
around them and becomes a center of

17
00:01:40,555 --> 00:01:48,000
attraction, a new center of power,
will immediately face repression,

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,215
even if they are not a politician—just
in case, to be safe. No

19
00:01:53,215 --> 00:01:57,000
gatherings of more than
three people, please.

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Fadeev told you to keep quiet.
Have another opinion? Keep quiet.

21
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:14,000
So, you ask me what will
happen and how. I think,

22
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:21,138
I can predict, or rather model, that
serious upheavals—geopolitical,

23
00:02:21,138 --> 00:02:27,436
no, social upheavals—in our
country will happen suddenly and

24
00:02:27,436 --> 00:02:33,000
spontaneously, as in the
February Revolution of 1917.

25
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:39,000
There was no bread, and women
in the queues began to grumble.

26
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:45,038
It happened so quickly that the
gendarmes and police, the tsar's

27
00:02:45,038 --> 00:02:49,000
secret police, did not
have time to react.

28
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:57,000
And suddenly it flared up. Then, like a
nuclear explosion, a chain reaction began.

29
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,549
I think something like that is likely.
It won't be like the example of

30
00:03:02,549 --> 00:03:08,098
Serbia we discussed: two years of
student struggle, an election, votes

31
00:03:08,098 --> 00:03:10,000
cast and new leadership.

32
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,882
No, that won't happen here.
Everything has been cleared away.

33
00:03:13,882 --> 00:03:17,000
Something spontaneous will
happen in the country.

34
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,742
What will trigger it? I can't
say; it could be anything. As for

35
00:03:21,742 --> 00:03:24,000
creating public organizations,

36
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:29,495
I have an idea for a virtual public
organization, because a real one

37
00:03:29,495 --> 00:03:32,000
would be shut down immediately.

38
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,900
Again, this isn't a political force
in the full sense. It doesn't mean

39
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:39,000
we can gather or hold actions.

40
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
None of that can be done in Russia now.

41
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,789
The communists did gather on
November 7, but that's an old story:

42
00:03:46,789 --> 00:03:49,000
they're given a certain quota.

43
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:57,160
Go on, gather with flags, sing Soviet
songs, chant something, but no

44
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:01,000
serious violations or criticism.

45
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,792
Whisper to one another, then sit in
the kitchen in the evening, drink

46
00:04:05,792 --> 00:04:11,000
to the motherland, drink to Stalin,
criticize the government and go to bed.

47
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,571
That's our plan for November 7.
A demonstration? God forbid! Red

48
00:04:15,571 --> 00:04:20,000
Square? A hundred, two hundred,
three hundred thousand people?

49
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:25,773
What are you thinking, Zyuganov? What
do you imagine you are? Have you

50
00:04:25,773 --> 00:04:28,000
forgotten our arrangements?

51
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:35,000
No moves like that. We gave you a quota and
seats in the State Duma, so enjoy them.

52
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Go on, imitate vigorous activity and
the defense of the working class.

53
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,336
Haven't we already jailed several of
your people as an example, so you

54
00:04:43,336 --> 00:04:46,000
understand that you
shouldn't joke with us?

55
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:52,634
Gather on Arbat Street, sing a few
songs, congratulate one another,

56
00:04:52,634 --> 00:04:56,000
stand under red flags and go home.

57
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
You see, friends, that's
essentially what is happening.

58
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:08,404
But I think some extraordinary,
unexpected event will happen, and what

59
00:05:08,404 --> 00:05:12,000
happened in 1917 will occur again.

60
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
It will start suddenly
in an unexpected place.

61
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:20,714
Could the tsar's secret police have
imagined that bread queues, made

62
00:05:20,714 --> 00:05:25,000
up mostly of women, would
trigger a chain reaction?

63
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:30,000
If they had, they would have dispersed the
queues or let people through one by one.

64
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:35,000
But they could not imagine it. They
had blocked everything they could.

65
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Still, it's impossible to
block absolutely everything.

66
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
And then, suddenly, it all exploded.

67
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,674
By the time they realized what
was happening, it was too late:

68
00:05:44,674 --> 00:05:49,000
soldiers, the garrison and workers had
joined in. It spread very quickly.

69
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,082
Naturally, people who had been
sitting and waiting for that moment

70
00:05:53,082 --> 00:05:55,000
immediately emerged to lead it.

71
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:59,000
In that case, it was the Russian
bourgeoisie. They had been waiting.

72
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
They too understood perfectly well that
things could not continue like that for long.

73
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
But they couldn't say it aloud; they
would have been suppressed too.

74
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
So they sat and waited.

75
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
When it happened, everything was ready.

76
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Everything was ready.

77
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Even the tsar's inner circle was ready.

78
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
They were waiting:

79
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,000
now we'll quickly arrange an
abdication, and off we go.

80
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
I think it will be similar here.

81
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:26,387
I am more than sure that many forces
at the top have already reached

82
00:06:26,387 --> 00:06:30,000
private agreements and are
waiting at the starting line.

83
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
They cannot speak openly;
they would be suppressed.

84
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
But they sit and wait.

85
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:41,000
And when something analogous to 1917
happens, they will immediately emerge,

86
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
because they will understand that's it:

87
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
it's your turn.

88
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
The boss will appear at the last moment,

89
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
and immediately a new boss will appear.

90
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,000
They'll quickly organize it,
lead it and enter government.

91
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
That's roughly how it will be.

92
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
That's my view.
